So what does that first report actually

283
00:09:59,300 --> 00:09:59,710
tell us?

284
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:02,450
It does not say where these objects came

285
00:10:02,470 --> 00:10:02,718
from.

286
00:10:03,188 --> 00:10:05,044
It says most were probably physical

287
00:10:05,064 --> 00:10:07,187
objects, that there are probably several

288
00:10:07,207 --> 00:10:09,331
kinds, and that the data was too thin to

289
00:10:09,351 --> 00:10:10,349
say what they were.

290
00:10:10,919 --> 00:10:12,976
144 reports.

291
00:10:13,316 --> 00:10:14,525
One explanation.

292
00:10:14,995 --> 00:10:17,134
And a government admitting, on paper, how

293
00:10:17,154 --> 00:10:18,241
much it did not know.

294
00:10:18,711 --> 00:10:20,870
Nine pages could not answer the question.

295
00:10:21,210 --> 00:10:22,669
But they put it on the record.

296
00:10:23,239 --> 00:10:25,109
Every secret has a release date.

297
00:10:25,529 --> 00:10:27,736
This one came with a line on page two.

298
00:10:28,318 --> 00:10:30,425
Data continues to be collected and

299
00:10:30,445 --> 00:10:30,988
analyzed.

300
00:10:31,809 --> 00:10:33,768
If there's a government file you want us

301
00:10:33,788 --> 00:10:35,402
to open, tell us in the comments.

302
00:10:35,972 --> 00:10:38,251
Next time: the night two hydrogen bombs

303
00:10:38,271 --> 00:10:39,608
fell on North Carolina.

304
00:10:39,948 --> 00:10:41,887
Goldsboro, 1961.
